---
/*
  /admin/writing/[id] — RETIRED as a page. The writing composer now lives in
  the WritingSheet overlay (docs/admin.md §5) so editing never navigates away
  from the list or the constellation composer. Old links still work: they land
  on the Fragment Manager with the sheet auto-opened via the hash.

  The target moved with the manager (`/admin` → `/admin/fragments`, ADR-0015).
  This redirect is a PRODUCER of that hash and had to be updated at source: a
  302 from `/admin` could not have carried it, because a hash never leaves the
  browser.
*/
/* Read inline rather than via a `const`. Astro's generated module reports a
   frontmatter binding used ONLY inside a top-level `return` as unused (ts6133),
   which is wrong but not suppressible — and a page this small does not need a
   name for a value it forwards once. */
return Astro.redirect(
  !Astro.params.id || Astro.params.id === 'new'
    ? '/admin/fragments#new-writing'
    : `/admin/fragments#edit=${Astro.params.id}`,
);
---
